{
  "name": "Win-Rate Champion Tiers",
  "author": "tardisdoctordalek",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "mod_type": "native",
  "contains_code": true,
  "description": "Builds an S/A/B/C/D champion tier list from in-game win-rate statistics and writes it to YOUR team only.\n\n== What is different ==\n1) Tiers are handed out by share of the ranked roster, not by fixed win-rate cut-offs. The win-rate metric pulls thin samples toward the break-even rate, so absolute cut-offs dump most of the roster into whichever band straddles it - which is why a threshold-based tier list ends up almost entirely B. Here the distribution is a config value: S/A/B/C/D shares default to 10/20/30/25/15 percent.\n\n2) The list is applied to your own team only. Writing one solved tier list to every AI team makes the whole league ban and pick the same champions, and the draft stops being interesting. Set apply_to_ai_teams=true if you want the old behaviour.\n\n== Composability ==\nThis mod registers a server extension and nothing else - no draft-score hook, no UI override. It does not take over the Champion screen, so it runs alongside a separate ban/pick mod without a load-order fight.\n\n== Config ==\nEdit config.ini next to the mod. Changes are hot-reloaded within a few management ticks; no restart needed. The mod also writes tier_table.txt (what it assigned and why) and schema_dump.txt (what it can see in the save) next to itself.",
  "last_updated": "2026-08-25",
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "mod_id": "base",
      "version": ">=0.5.6"
    }
  ]
}
